 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** The derivation of $c_{00}$ relies on the assumption that pixel RGB is a strong observation of base appearance [S1, unofficial]. If lighting conditions vary significantly or if the pixel does not correspond to a single Gaussian (e.g., occlusion), this training-free derivation may introduce artifacts [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Precision:** The derivation of $c_{00}$ relies on the assumption that pixel RGB is a strong observation of base appearance [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Boundaries:** The validity mask in WCM computation uses $\mathbb{I}[u \in \Omega]$ to handle points falling outside the image domain [S1, unofficial]. Points with $z \le 0$ are also masked out [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** The method assumes unposed images [S1, unofficial]. If poses are known, the camera estimation head may still function but the pose-free advantage is lost [S1, unofficial]. The masked attention mechanism prevents target-view information from affecting Gaussian reconstruction, which is critical when $N_T > 0$ [S1, unofficial].
